    "review": {
      "player_and_trigger": "The player trigger explicitly includes targets treated as staggered by an effect. This matches MinionState.is_staggered, which returns true for either a live stagger count or count_as_staggered keyword. The predicate reads params.attacked_unit when the blessing event is checked; it does not use the separate before-attack snapshot. All other trigger/action timing conclusions remain accepted.",
      "traits_bindings_and_ui": "The map has exactly the two actual trait variants and five bindings: combatknife_p1 M1/M2 and ogryn_club_p2 M1/M2/M3. The five displayed weapon names and mark associations match the scoped weapon metadata and UI receipt.",
      "tier_child_and_lifecycle": "All four tiers are +0.125/+0.15/+0.175/+0.20 melee critical-chance inputs. The child conditional generic critical_strike_chance tier override replaces its 0.10 fallback; it is not an additional 0.10. Child duration is 4.5 seconds; raw cap 2 with max_stacks=1 and offset=-1 yields one effective layer. A qualifying active hit that adds zero still refreshes the timer. Held-slot gating suspends the bonus while switching away, the timer continues, and unequipping removes the trait state.",
      "action_start_and_profiles": "ActionSweep saves the critical flag at action start; the trigger hit cannot retroactively change its result and other hits in that same action use the saved flag. Ordinary attacks and pure pushes do not trigger or refresh. The three club marks have qualifying special slaps. The Mk II special-chain follow-up punch has a weapon-special profile and can qualify; Mk IIIb uses the same-named ordinary punch profile and cannot trigger.",
      "math_and_formatting": "The stated examples correctly distinguish percentage-point additions from relative chance increases (20 pp is +400% relative to a 5% input; with q=10 pp it changes 15% to 35%, +133.33% relative). The formula clamps the additive chance before applying chance-to-damage conversion, with stated assumptions.",
      "raw_and_errata": "English and Traditional Chinese description strings remain exact and paired to the same keys/hashes. The four tier reconstructions substitute the verified formatter values. Omitted mechanics are labeled as not covered by the localization; no unsupported erratum is asserted.",
      "icons_and_reverse_indexes": "Combat Blade uses weapon_trait_198 and Bully Club uses weapon_trait_211 with their distinct verified attachment URLs. The blessing map, blessing/melee directories, both weapon reverse pages, and the new Bully Club reverse page point to the correct entry and variant pages."
    },
